  "cover_text": "In a small bowl, combine fennel, capers, paprika, cinnamon, allspice, and thyme. Stir in crushed tomatoes and tomato sauce. Add green beans, mix, and cook over high heat until beans start to soften, about 8 minutes. Serving: Adjust seasoning to taste. Heat sugar to a six inch heat. Fill zaxis with green beans. Add more sugar if the beans start to look overcooked (about 4 inches). Cover and cook for another 3 minutes. Remove zaxis from heat and stir in these ingredients: ½ garlic, ¼ onion, ½ paprika, 2 finely sliced oranges, 40-thousand grains, 1 green pepper, 2 bay leaves, salt, pepper. Add lemon juice, stir well, and let stand a bit. Serve with",
